WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.840
. There's been a super interesting turn of
events in the last 48 hours or so where Donald

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.191
Trump has called Fox News fake news at a recent
event.

00:00:09.191 --> 00:00:17.810
And after day one of the DNC, multiple Fox
News anchors actually heaped praise upon Michelle

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.080
Obama for her speech, which was a good speech.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.689
So let's not read into this more than what
it is.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.939
But I do think there's an interesting discussion
here.

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:32.090
Here's Donald Trump in Wisconsin this week
calling Fox News fake news.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.200
But we're doing great.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.460
Coming back, we're coming back.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.070
And our numbers are better than almost all
countries.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.309
I will tell you that despite what you hear.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:42.170
Look at all of them up there, Scott.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.640
Look at all of that fake news.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.390
It's unbelievable.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.989
Unfortunately, Fox has become vague.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:50.740
Still, I don't know what happens to these
people.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.740
Right.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.740
You agree.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:57.690
And then continuing the reversals behavior
that is opposite what we would expect.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.239
What we've come to expect on Monday night.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:03.829
Check out Dana Perino, Chris Wallace.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:08.390
People liked Michelle Obama's speech on Fox
News over the course of the night, the first

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.340
virtual convention of our history.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.040
I think they would say that Michelle Obama
stuck the landing.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.470
Chris Wallace, your thought.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.409
Well, I agree with Dana.

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:22.799
You know, it's interesting, Michelle Obama,
as she said, doesn't like politics.

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:27.730
And she said that this speech was her main
contribution to the Biden campaign.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:29.509
It was a heck of a contribution.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:36.130
She really slayed, sliced and diced Donald
Trump talking about the chaos and confusion

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:41.360
and lack of empathy, especially coming from
this president and from this White House,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:45.979
spoke more about the deficits of Donald Trump
than the pluses of Joe Biden.

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:49.040
But didn't talk about especially on some of
his policies.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.909
But especially his empathy, what he's been
through and his care for average American

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:55.479
troops that we have to vote.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:56.660
So what do we make of this?

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:03.799
Is this some major reversal where Fox News
is no longer right wing and no longer supporting

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:06.689
Trump and Fox News now supports Democrats?

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:10.980
No, no, no, no, no, not not even in the slightest.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:16.450
It's a very instructive example to understand
a little bit about how corporate media works

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.860
in the United States.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:24.890
Fox News offers theatrics and hyperbole from
a right wing perspective for profit.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:27.830
And the for profit part is a big piece of
the analysis.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:33.780
So think back to early in the 2016 Republican
primary, which started in 2015.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:41.170
Really, the role of Fox News was we covered
Trump being kooky, but we oppose him because

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:45.090
we're a serious right wing network and we
support people like, you know, whoever the

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.980
buttoned up right winger was at the time.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.080
Was it jab or was it, you know, Ted Cruz or
whatever?

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.310
Doesn't matter.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:56.360
Trump then wins the primary, then FOX News
falls in line and gets behind Donald Trump

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.350
because they're not going to get behind Hillary
Clinton.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.600
Hillary's bad.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:00.600
Obama's bad.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:01.720
They get behind Trump.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:06.000
And it is a business decision fundamentally
and a decision about if Trump is president.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.040
I mean, he's the nominee.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.600
If he's president, we want access to Trump.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.070
Trump becomes president and is completely
outrageous as president.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:18.210
So Fox News actually sort of does a Dr. Jekyll
and Mr. Hyde sort of thing.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:23.860
The opinion people remain solidly behind Trump
carrying water for him.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:30.700
You know, Sean Hannity, Jeanine Pirro, Laura
Ingraham, Tucker Carlson, mostly the Fox and

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.100
Friends, people who I know that's supposedly
a news show.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.100
Come on, guys.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.100
That's an opinion show.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:40.230
But they do want to gin up controversy and
kind of play all sides.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.840
So when Shep Smith still worked at the network,
he would sometimes call out Trump for his

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:50.040
obvious lies or Chris Wallace will confront
Trump during interviews or whatever the case

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.040
may be.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.930
OK, now we find ourselves in a situation where
it's unclear if Donald Trump is going to win.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:00.930
So Fox is running parallel narratives, again,
for profit.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:06.930
This is what explains the entire sort of status
quo at Fox News, Hannity and the opinion.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:10.340
People are mostly still behind Trump.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:16.030
If Trump wins, Trump will still be there for
them and they'll be there for Trump if Donald

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.290
Trump is reelected.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:22.110
If Trump loses, Fox is laying out a little
bit of the groundwork.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.720
They're laying a little pipe, so to speak,
to say we're objective.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.940
We criticize Trump or praised Democrats like
Michelle Obama's speech when it made sense.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.760
And the point is to be positioned after November
for any eventuality to maintain access to

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.650
people in positions of power.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:41.650
Period.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:48.090
Now, you might be wondering, does do Fox executives
pull Chris Wallace aside and go, listen, Chris,

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:54.940
we need you to praise Michelle Obama and really
be tough on Trump so that we can do this plan?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.370
No, that's not the way it works.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:01.450
It's much the same way as, you know, our TV
anchors will often say, I actually haven't

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.980
seen Archie in years, but years ago, I don't
even know if it's still on TV in the U.S.,

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:05.980
honestly.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:11.730
But but years ago, Archie anchors would say,
I've never been told what to say on the air

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:14.540
in terms of Russia narratives or whatever.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.830
That's not the way it works.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.830
Right.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:20.880
You are selected because you have been hired
in a role.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.880
Right.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:28.590
You you are choosing the people that on their
own will play the roles that you are trying

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.590
to fill.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.830
And it's much the same thing on Fox News.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.810
So I don't believe it's calculated in that
Chris Wallace needs to be told what to do.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:38.101
Chris Wallace just needs to be put in positions
to do what Chris Wallace does, and that's

00:05:38.101 --> 00:05:39.140
how they build the narrative.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.460
So the bottom line is money.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.460
That's really it.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:43.920
The Murdoch family isn't stupid.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.530
The big goal is to be in line with conservative
governments.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.910
Be friendly with right wing governments around
the world.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:06:00.060
If they can help the right retain its power,
then they will swing some support to whoever

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.980
is likely to win.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.340
And that's the strategy.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:09.080
If it looks like the right will lose power,
then they will put a little bit of support

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.260
just enough behind whoever is likely to win.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.990
So that when that person wins, be it Joe Biden.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:18.660
Or were it Hillary Clinton in 2016?

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:25.680
They can maintain access and they can kind
of create a responsibility from the winner

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:31.730
to still treat Fox News seriously, because
that's how Fox News continues to sort of replicate

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.190
itself and perpetuate itself.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.540
This is business one to one.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.950
You might notice there is no journalism analysis
here.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:43.060
This is not a communications analysis where
you would understand, you know, in a in a

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:48.570
theoretical academic communication class about
anything related to journalism or media.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:49.620
This is business.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.780
This is what you would learn in business school.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:55.820
And if you try to evaluate this as journalism.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.470
The commentary makes no sense.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:02.121
If you see this through the lens of business,
then it makes perfect sense.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:05.790
And that's exactly what this is for Fox News.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.970
Don't be tricked into thinking that it's anything
else.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:14.590
We'll have more coverage of this on the show's
Instagram The David Pakman Show on Instagram.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:08:26.889
And while you're there, you can follow me
on Instagram at David Dot

00:08:26.889 --> 00:08:29.080
Packman as well.

